      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COLOURS OF AUTUMN (3) gets top billing after two narrow thirds this campaign, the latest at this track when beaten just under a length in Open grade. She drops into BM70 company, has a one-from-three record at this track and distance, and the 2kg claim adds to a solid winning case. SAND 'N' POWER (1) is the main danger after arriving in time to beat Russian Summer here last start in a CL4. He rises in weight, but his three wins and one placing from four runs at this venue make him a serious threat again. SINGULAR (7) was below market expectation as favourite here last time, though the steadied run late gives him some excuse, and his track-and-distance record keeps him in the mix. FANCY GARTER (6) brings winning form from Cooktown and drops sharply in weight, with her strong season profile offset by the harder assignment from BM55 grade. KICKOFF (8) is knocking on the door of another win and doesn't have to improve much to land the winning blow.",
